  "ingredients": [
    "12 ounce chicken sausage",
    "6 ounce cremini mushrooms",
    "3 cup spinach",
    "10 large egg",
    "1 tablespoon ranch dressing",
    "2 teaspoon hot sauce",
    "1/2 teaspoon all-purpose seasoning (such as Mrs. Dash)",
    "1 1/2 cup cheddar cheese (shredded)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 400F. Thinly slice the sausages and mushrooms.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata/#wprm-recipe-50781-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Start by adding the sausages to a cast-iron skillet over medium-high heat — wait until the cast iron is thoroughly heated through before adding the sausages.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata/#wprm-recipe-50781-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the sausages are cooking, chop up the spinach. Just a rough chop will do; no need to get fancy.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata/#wprm-recipe-50781-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": null
    },
    {
      "text": "When the sausages are crisp on one side, flip them over and add the mushrooms and spinach.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata/#wprm-recipe-50781-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the spinach and mushrooms are cooking, crack the eggs into a container and add the ranch, hot sauce, and seasoning. Whisk together well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata/#wprm-recipe-50781-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the sausages, spinach, and mushrooms to enable the spinach to wilt fully. Add salt and pepper to taste.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata/#wprm-recipe-50781-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata11.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the spinach is fully wilted, add the cheese on top.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata/#wprm-recipe-50781-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata12.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour the eggs over the mixture and mix everything together well. Make sure that the eggs are touching the bottom of the pan — lift the other ingredients if needed.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata/#wprm-recipe-50781-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata14.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let the mixture cook for a moment and then place the cast-iron skillet in the oven. Bake for 10 minutes, then broil for 3–4 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata/#wprm-recipe-50781-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata16.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the oven and let cool for 10 minutes. Slice and serve!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata/#wprm-recipe-50781-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/cast-iron-kitchen-sink-frittata17.jpg"
    }
  ],
